{"task_id": "Mbpp/57", "solution": "def find_Max_Num(digits: list[int]) -> int:\n    # Convert digits to strings for comparison and concatenation.\n    # A custom comparison function is used to sort the string representations of digits such that\n    # concatenating them in this order forms the largest number.\n    str_digits = [str(d) for d in digits]\n\n    def compare(s1, s2):\n        if s1 + s2 > s2 + s1:\n            return -1  # s1 should come before s2\n        elif s1 + s2 < s2 + s1:\n            return 1   # s2 should come before s1\n        else:\n            return 0\n\n    # Sort the string digits using the custom comparison.\n    # The functools.cmp_to_key is used to convert the comparison function to a key function.\n    import functools\n    str_digits.sort(key=functools.cmp_to_key(compare))\n\n    # Join the sorted strings and convert to an integer.\n    # Handle the case of an empty list or a list of zeros.\n    if not str_digits or str_digits[0] == '0':\n        return 0\n    \n    return int(\"\".join(str_digits))"}
