{"task_id": "Mbpp/61", "solution": "def count_Substrings(input_string: str) -> int:\n    total_count = 0\n    n = len(input_string)\n\n    # Iterate over all possible starting indices of substrings\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_sum = 0\n        # Iterate over all possible ending indices of substrings starting from 'i'\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            # Calculate the sum of digits for the current substring\n            current_sum += int(input_string[j])\n            # Calculate the length of the current substring\n            current_length = j - i + 1\n            \n            # Check if the sum of digits equals the length\n            if current_sum == current_length:\n                total_count += 1\n    return total_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/63", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple, Union\nNumber = Union[int, float]\ndef max_difference(tuple_list: List[Tuple[Number, Number]]) -> Number:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum absolute difference between elements within pairs\n    in a given list of tuples. Returns 0 if the input list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not tuple_list:\n        return 0\n\n    max_diff = 0\n    for element1, element2 in tuple_list:\n        current_diff = abs(element1 - element2)\n        if current_diff > max_diff:\n            max_diff = current_diff\n    return max_diff"}
