{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "from typing import List, Dict, Optional\nclass PatternMapping:\n    \"\"\"Manages the one-to-one bidirectional mapping between pattern elements and words.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._element_to_word: Dict[str, str] = {}\n        self._word_to_element: Dict[str, str] = {}\n\n    def add_mapping(self, element: str, word: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Attempts to add a new mapping or verifies an existing one.\n        Returns True if the mapping is consistent, False otherwise.\n        \"\"\"\n        # Check consistency for pattern element\n        if element in self._element_to_word:\n            if self._element_to_word[element] != word:\n                return False\n\n        # Check consistency for word\n        if word in self._word_to_element:\n            if self._word_to_element[word] != element:\n                return False\n\n        # If consistent, add/update mappings\n        self._element_to_word[element] = word\n        self._word_to_element[word] = element\n        return True\n\n    def get_word_for_element(self, element: str) -> Optional[str]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves the word mapped to a given pattern element, or None if not found.\"\"\"\n        return self._element_to_word.get(element)\n\n    def get_element_for_word(self, word: str) -> Optional[str]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves the pattern element mapped to a given word, or None if not found.\"\"\"\n        return self._word_to_element.get(word)\ndef is_samepatterns(words: List[str], pattern: List[str]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if the 'words' list follows the 'pattern' list based on a one-to-one mapping\n    and sequence adherence.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(words) != len(pattern):\n        return False\n\n    mapper = PatternMapping()\n\n    for i in range(len(words)):\n        current_word = words[i]\n        current_pattern_element = pattern[i]\n\n        if not mapper.add_mapping(current_pattern_element, current_word):\n            return False # Inconsistent mapping found\n\n    return True"}
