{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "class NewmanConwayCalculator:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates Newman-Conway sequence numbers using memoization.\n    Stores previously computed values to avoid redundant calculations.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._memo = {1: 1, 2: 1}\n\n    def calculate(self, n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the nth Newman-Conway number.\n        The sequence is P(n) = P(P(n-1)) + P(n - P(n-1)) for n > 2.\n        \"\"\"\n        if n in self._memo:\n            return self._memo[n]\n\n        # Iteratively calculate values from 3 up to n, ensuring all required sub-problems are computed.\n        for i in range(3, n + 1):\n            if i not in self._memo:\n                p_i_minus_1_val = self._memo[i - 1]\n                term1_idx = p_i_minus_1_val\n                term2_idx = i - p_i_minus_1_val\n                self._memo[i] = self._memo[term1_idx] + self._memo[term2_idx]\n\n        return self._memo[n]\n_newman_conway_calculator = NewmanConwayCalculator()\ndef sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence using a memoized calculator.\n    \"\"\"\n    return _newman_conway_calculator.calculate(n)"}
