{"task_id": "Mbpp/131", "solution": "VOWELS_SET = {'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'}\ndef _is_vowel(char: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a character is a vowel (case-insensitive, 'y' excluded).\"\"\"\n    return char.lower() in VOWELS_SET\ndef reverse_vowels(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Reverses only the vowels of a given string, keeping non-vowel characters in place.\n    \"\"\"\n    char_list = list(s)\n    \n    # Collect all vowels from the string in their original order\n    vowels_in_order = []\n    for char in char_list:\n        if _is_vowel(char):\n            vowels_in_order.append(char)\n            \n    # Reverse the collected vowels for placement\n    vowels_in_order.reverse() \n    \n    # Replace the original vowel positions with the reversed vowels\n    vowel_ptr = 0\n    for i in range(len(char_list)):\n        if _is_vowel(char_list[i]):\n            char_list[i] = vowels_in_order[vowel_ptr]\n            vowel_ptr += 1\n            \n    return \"\".join(char_list)"}
