{"task_id": "Mbpp/133", "solution": "def sum_negativenum(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of negative numbers from a list using domain-driven design principles.\n    It encapsulates number logic and list management within helper classes defined inline.\"\"\"\n\n    class Number:\n        def __init__(self, value: int):\n            self._value = value\n        \n        def is_negative(self) -> bool:\n            return self._value < 0\n        \n        def get_value(self) -> int:\n            return self._value\n\n    class NumberList:\n        def __init__(self, numbers: list[int] = None):\n            self._numbers: list[Number] = []\n            if numbers is not None:\n                for num_value in numbers:\n                    self.add_number(num_value)\n        \n        def add_number(self, number_value: int):\n            self._numbers.append(Number(number_value))\n        \n        def get_negative_numbers(self) -> list[Number]:\n            return [num_obj for num_obj in self._numbers if num_obj.is_negative()]\n\n    number_list_instance = NumberList(numbers)\n    negative_number_objects = number_list_instance.get_negative_numbers()\n    \n    total_sum = 0\n    for num_obj in negative_number_objects:\n        total_sum += num_obj.get_value()\n        \n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/137", "solution": "def zero_count(numbers: list[int]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the ratio of zeroes to non-zeroes in a list of integers.\n    Returns 0.0 if there are no non-zero elements to prevent division by zero.\"\"\"\n\n    def _get_zero_count(nums: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Counts the number of zero elements in the input list.\"\"\"\n        count = 0\n        for num in nums:\n            if num == 0:\n                count += 1\n        return count\n\n    def _get_non_zero_count(nums: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Counts the number of non-zero elements in the input list.\"\"\"\n        count = 0\n        for num in nums:\n            if num != 0:\n                count += 1\n        return count\n\n    zeroes = _get_zero_count(numbers)\n    non_zeroes = _get_non_zero_count(numbers)\n\n    if non_zeroes == 0:\n        return 0.0\n    else:\n        return float(zeroes) / non_zeroes"}
