{"task_id": "Mbpp/233", "solution": "def lateralsuface_cylinder(radius: float, height: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the lateral surface area of a cylinder.\n    This function uses an inline Cylinder class for its core logic.\n    \"\"\"\n    import math\n\n    class Cylinder:\n        \"\"\"\n        Encapsulates the radius and height of a cylinder and provides\n        the method to calculate its lateral surface area.\n        \"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, radius: float, height: float):\n            self._radius = radius\n            self._height = height\n\n        @property\n        def radius(self) -> float:\n            return self._radius\n\n        @property\n        def height(self) -> float:\n            return self._height\n\n        def calculate_lateral_surface_area(self) -> float:\n            return 2 * math.pi * self._radius * self._height\n\n    cylinder = Cylinder(radius, height)\n    return cylinder.calculate_lateral_surface_area()"}
