{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    # Validate inputs m and n according to BR5 and BR6\n    if not (isinstance(m, int) and m > 0):\n        raise ValueError(\"m must be a positive integer.\")\n    if not (isinstance(n, int) and n > 0):\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    # Base case for sequence length 1 (BR1)\n    if n == 1:\n        return m\n\n    # Memoization table to store results of subproblems: memo[(length_remaining, min_possible_current_element)]\n    memo = {}\n\n    def count_sequences_recursive(length_remaining: int, min_val_for_current_element: int) -> int:\n        # If the minimum required value exceeds m, no valid sequence can be formed (BR4)\n        if min_val_for_current_element > m:\n            return 0\n        \n        # If we have calculated this state before, return the memoized result\n        if (length_remaining, min_val_for_current_element) in memo:\n            return memo[(length_remaining, min_val_for_current_element)]\n\n        # Base case for recursion: if only one element is remaining\n        if length_remaining == 1:\n            # Number of valid values for the last element: from min_val_for_current_element to m (inclusive)\n            # Each element must be a positive integer (BR2)\n            result = max(0, m - min_val_for_current_element + 1)\n            memo[(length_remaining, min_val_for_current_element)] = result\n            return result\n\n        total_sub_sequences = 0\n        # Iterate through possible values for the current element (BR2, BR4)\n        for current_element_val in range(min_val_for_current_element, m + 1):\n            # Recursively find sequences for the remaining length, ensuring the next element is at least twice the current (BR3)\n            total_sub_sequences += count_sequences_recursive(length_remaining - 1, 2 * current_element_val)\n        \n        # Store the computed result in the memoization table\n        memo[(length_remaining, min_val_for_current_element)] = total_sub_sequences\n        return total_sub_sequences\n\n    total_sequences = 0\n    # Iterate through all possible values for the first element of the sequence (BR2, BR4)\n    # The first element can be any integer from 1 to m\n    for first_element in range(1, m + 1):\n        # Calculate sequences for the remaining n-1 length, where the next element must be at least 2 * first_element\n        total_sequences += count_sequences_recursive(n - 1, 2 * first_element)\n\n    return total_sequences"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "def max_sum(arr: list[int | float]) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence in the given array.\n    A bitonic subsequence is first increasing and then decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return arr[0]\n\n    # Calculate LIS (Longest Increasing Subsequence) sums\n    # lis_sums[i] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at index i\n    lis_sums = [0] * n\n    for i in range(n):\n        lis_sums[i] = arr[i]\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                lis_sums[i] = max(lis_sums[i], lis_sums[j] + arr[i])\n\n    # Calculate LDS (Longest Decreasing Subsequence) sums\n    # lds_sums[i] stores the maximum sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at index i\n    lds_sums = [0] * n\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        lds_sums[i] = arr[i]\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                lds_sums[i] = max(lds_sums[i], lds_sums[j] + arr[i])\n\n    # Combine LIS and LDS sums to find the maximum bitonic sum\n    # A bitonic subsequence with arr[i] as peak is lis_sums[i] + lds_sums[i] - arr[i]\n    max_bitonic_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        # We subtract arr[i] once because it's included in both lis_sums[i] and lds_sums[i]\n        current_bitonic_sum = lis_sums[i] + lds_sums[i] - arr[i]\n        max_bitonic_sum = max(max_bitonic_sum, current_bitonic_sum)\n\n    return max_bitonic_sum"}
