{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the given string.\n    Uses dynamic programming to build up solutions for substrings.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n\n    # An empty string has an LPS length of 0.\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the longest palindromic subsequence\n    # for the substring s[i...j].\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # All single characters are palindromic subsequences of length 1.\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table for lengths from 2 to n.\n    # 'length' represents the length of the current substring.\n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            j = i + length - 1\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                # If the characters at the ends match, they extend the palindrome\n                # formed by the inner substring s[i+1...j-1].\n                # dp[i+1][j-1] would be 0 if length is 2 (i+1 > j-1), effectively adding 2 to 0.\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i+1][j-1]\n            else:\n                # If the characters at the ends do not match,\n                # the LPS is either by excluding s[i] or excluding s[j].\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i+1][j], dp[i][j-1])\n\n    # The result for the entire string s is stored in dp[0][n-1].\n    return dp[0][n-1]"}
