{"task_id": "Mbpp/260", "solution": "def newman_prime(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth Newman-Shanks-Williams number S_n and verifies if it is prime.\n    If S_n is not prime, it raises an error.\"\"\"\n\n    def is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if a given number is a prime number using trial division.\"\"\"\n        if num < 2:\n            return False\n        if num == 2 or num == 3:\n            return True\n        if num % 2 == 0 or num % 3 == 0:\n            return False\n        i = 5\n        while i * i <= num:\n            if num % i == 0 or num % (i + 2) == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 6\n        return True\n\n    def calculate_nsw_term(k: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Computes the kth term of the Newman-Shanks-Williams sequence (S_k).\"\"\"\n        if k == 0:\n            return 1\n        if k == 1:\n            return 1\n        \n        s_prev2 = 1  # S_0\n        s_prev1 = 1  # S_1\n        \n        for _ in range(2, k + 1):\n            s_current = 2 * s_prev1 + s_prev2\n            s_prev2 = s_prev1\n            s_prev1 = s_current\n        return s_prev1\n    \n    s_n = calculate_nsw_term(n)\n    \n    if is_prime(s_n):\n        return s_n\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(\"S_n is not prime\")"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/265", "solution": "def list_split(input_list: list, n: int) -> list[list]:\n    \"\"\"Splits an input list into n sublists, distributing elements by index modulo n.\"\"\"\n    output_list = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n\n    for i, item in enumerate(input_list):\n        sublist_index = i % n\n        output_list[sublist_index].append(item)\n\n    return output_list"}
