{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr: list[int], k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest sum of a contiguous sub-array in the modified array,\n    which is formed by repeating the given array k times.\n    \"\"\"\n    import math\n\n    def _kadane(arr_inner: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum of a contiguous sub-array using Kadane's algorithm.\"\"\"\n        if not arr_inner:\n            return 0\n        \n        max_current = arr_inner[0]\n        max_global = arr_inner[0]\n        \n        for i in range(1, len(arr_inner)):\n            max_current = max(arr_inner[i], max_current + arr_inner[i])\n            max_global = max(max_global, max_current)\n            \n        return max_global\n\n    def _calculate_total_sum(arr_inner: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all elements in the given array.\"\"\"\n        return sum(arr_inner)\n\n    def _calculate_max_prefix_sum(arr_inner: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the maximum prefix sum of the given array.\"\"\"\n        if not arr_inner:\n            return 0\n        current_sum = 0\n        max_prefix = -math.inf\n        for x in arr_inner:\n            current_sum += x\n            max_prefix = max(max_prefix, current_sum)\n        return max_prefix\n\n    def _calculate_max_suffix_sum(arr_inner: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the maximum suffix sum of the given array.\"\"\"\n        if not arr_inner:\n            return 0\n        current_sum = 0\n        max_suffix = -math.inf\n        for x in reversed(arr_inner):\n            current_sum += x\n            max_suffix = max(max_suffix, current_sum)\n        return max_suffix\n\n    # Step 1: Calculate max subarray sum for a single instance of arr\n    max_sum_single_array = _kadane(arr)\n\n    # If k is 1, the result is simply the max subarray sum of the original array\n    if k == 1:\n        return max_sum_single_array\n\n    # If k > 1, we need to consider cases where the subarray spans across repetitions\n    total_sum_arr = _calculate_total_sum(arr)\n    max_prefix = _calculate_max_prefix_sum(arr)\n    max_suffix = _calculate_max_suffix_sum(arr)\n\n    # Initialize overall maximum with the best sum from a single repetition\n    overall_max = max_sum_single_array\n\n    # Case 2: Max subarray spans across two concatenated arrays (e.g., suffix of first + prefix of second)\n    overall_max = max(overall_max, max_prefix + max_suffix)\n\n    # Case 3: Max subarray spans across multiple full repetitions (more than two)\n    # This is only beneficial if the total sum of 'arr' is positive.\n    if total_sum_arr > 0 and k > 2:\n        max_sum_repeated_middle = total_sum_arr * (k - 2) + max_prefix + max_suffix\n        overall_max = max(overall_max, max_sum_repeated_middle)\n\n    return overall_max"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/290", "solution": "def max_length(list_of_lists: list[list]) -> tuple[int, list]:\n    \"\"\"Finds the list of maximum length in a list of lists.\n\n    Args:\n        list_of_lists: A list where each element is itself a list.\n\n    Returns:\n        A tuple containing the maximum length found and the first list\n        that has this maximum length.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_len = 0\n    max_list = None\n\n    for sub_list in list_of_lists:\n        current_len = len(sub_list)\n        if current_len > max_len:\n            max_len = current_len\n            max_list = sub_list\n            \n    return (max_len, max_list)"}
