{"task_id": "Mbpp/300", "solution": "import math\ndef count_binary_seq(n: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the count of binary sequences of length 2n where the sum of the first n bits\n    equals the sum of the last n bits. This count is given by the central binomial coefficient C(2n, n).\n    \"\"\"\n    # The number of ways to choose k '1's in the first n bits is C(n, k).\n    # The number of ways to choose k '1's in the last n bits is C(n, k).\n    # Summing C(n, k) * C(n, k) for k from 0 to n equals C(2n, n).\n    return float(math.comb(2 * n, n))"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/301", "solution": "def dict_depth(input_dict: dict) -> int:\n    # Base case: if the dictionary is empty or contains no nested dictionaries, its depth is 1.\n    if not isinstance(input_dict, dict):\n        return 0 # Or handle as an error if input_dict must always be a dictionary\n    \n    max_depth = 0\n    for value in input_dict.values():\n        if isinstance(value, dict):\n            max_depth = max(max_depth, dict_depth(value))\n    \n    return 1 + max_depth"}
