{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "def max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr: list[int], n: int, i: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence from arr[0...i]\n    where all elements are less than arr[k], then adds arr[k] to this sum.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _validate_inputs(arr_len: int, i_idx: int, k_idx: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Validates input indices for bounds and k_idx > i_idx.\"\"\"\n        if not (0 <= i_idx < arr_len and 0 <= k_idx < arr_len):\n            raise ValueError(\"Indices i or k are out of bounds.\")\n        if k_idx <= i_idx:\n            raise ValueError(\"Index k must be greater than index i.\")\n\n    def _find_max_increasing_subsequence_sum_filtered(elements: list[int], upper_bound: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Computes the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence from 'elements',\n        where each element in the subsequence must be less than 'upper_bound'.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not elements:\n            return 0\n\n        dp = [0] * len(elements)\n        max_sum_so_far = 0\n\n        for j in range(len(elements)):\n            # Per design, explicitly check against upper_bound even if elements are pre-filtered.\n            if elements[j] < upper_bound:\n                dp[j] = elements[j]\n                for p in range(j):\n                    # Per design, explicitly check against upper_bound even if elements are pre-filtered.\n                    if elements[j] > elements[p] and elements[p] < upper_bound:\n                        dp[j] = max(dp[j], dp[p] + elements[j])\n                max_sum_so_far = max(max_sum_so_far, dp[j])\n        return max_sum_so_far\n\n    _validate_inputs(n, i, k)\n\n    val_k = arr[k]\n    \n    # Extract prefix arr[0...i]\n    prefix_arr = arr[0 : i + 1]\n\n    # Filter prefix elements to include only those less than arr[k]\n    filtered_prefix = [x for x in prefix_arr if x < val_k]\n\n    # Calculate Max Sum Increasing Subsequence from Filtered Prefix\n    max_prefix_subsequence_sum = _find_max_increasing_subsequence_sum_filtered(filtered_prefix, val_k)\n\n    # Add arr[k] to the subsequence sum\n    final_sum = max_prefix_subsequence_sum + val_k\n\n    return final_sum"}
