{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "def set_left_most_unset_bit(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the left-most unset bit in n (most significant 0-bit within its magnitude) and sets it.\n    If no such bit is found within n's magnitude, returns n unchanged.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Determine the highest bit position relevant to n's magnitude.\n    # For n=10 (0b1010), bit_length() is 4, so msb_pos is 3.\n    msb_pos = n.bit_length() - 1\n\n    # Iterate from the most significant bit position downwards to find the left-most unset bit.\n    for k in range(msb_pos, -1, -1):\n        # Check if the k-th bit is unset (0).\n        if not (n & (1 << k)):\n            # If unset, set this bit and return the modified number.\n            return n | (1 << k)\n\n    # If the loop completes, all bits up to msb_pos were set (e.g., n=7).\n    # In this case, return the original number as per design.\n    return n"}
