{"task_id": "Mbpp/410", "solution": "def min_val(input_list: list) -> (int | float):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum numeric value in a heterogeneous list.\n    Non-numeric elements are ignored.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _is_numeric(element: object) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if an element is an integer or a float.\"\"\"\n        return isinstance(element, (int, float))\n\n    def _filter_numeric_elements(lst: list) -> list:\n        \"\"\"Filters a list to include only numeric elements.\"\"\"\n        return [element for element in lst if _is_numeric(element)]\n\n    numeric_elements = _filter_numeric_elements(input_list)\n\n    # Assumes there will always be at least one numeric element as per problem statement and assert\n    return min(numeric_elements)"}
