{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "def max_Product(arr: list[int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds a pair of integers from the given array with the highest product.\n    Assumes the input array contains at least two integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    arr.sort()\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    # Product of the two largest numbers\n    product_of_largest_two = arr[n - 1] * arr[n - 2]\n\n    # Product of the two smallest numbers (important for negative numbers)\n    product_of_smallest_two = arr[0] * arr[1]\n\n    if product_of_largest_two >= product_of_smallest_two:\n        return (arr[n - 2], arr[n - 1])\n    else:\n        return (arr[0], arr[1])"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/418", "solution": "def Find_Max(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Finds the element (sub-list) with the maximum length in a list of lists.\n    Returns the sub-list with the maximum length, or an empty list if input is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    max_length = -1\n    max_element = None\n\n    for sub_list in input_list:\n        current_length = len(sub_list)\n\n        if current_length >= max_length:\n            max_length = current_length\n            max_element = sub_list\n\n    return max_element"}
