{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "class PerrinSequenceCalculator:\n    \"\"\"Calculates Perrin numbers and their sums using memoization.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the calculator with base Perrin numbers.\"\"\"\n        self._memo: dict[int, int] = {\n            0: 3,\n            1: 0,\n            2: 2\n        }\n\n    def calculate_perrin(self, index: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the Perrin number for a given index P(index).\"\"\"\n        if index in self._memo:\n            return self._memo[index]\n\n        # For n > 2, P(n) = P(n-2) + P(n-3)\n        perrin_n = self.calculate_perrin(index - 2) + self.calculate_perrin(index - 3)\n        self._memo[index] = perrin_n\n        return perrin_n\n\n    def calculate_sum(self, max_index: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of Perrin numbers from P(0) to P(max_index) (inclusive).\"\"\"\n        total_sum = 0\n        for i in range(max_index + 1):\n            total_sum += self.calculate_perrin(i)\n        return total_sum\ndef cal_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of Perrin numbers from P(0) to P(n) (inclusive).\n    It uses a memoized calculator for efficiency.\n    \"\"\"\n    calculator = PerrinSequenceCalculator()\n    return calculator.calculate_sum(n)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/453", "solution": "def sumofFactors(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all even factors of a given number.\n    It iterates from 1 up to the number and adds even factors to a running total.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i in range(1, number + 1):\n        if number % i == 0 and i % 2 == 0:\n            total_sum += i\n    return total_sum"}
