{"task_id": "Mbpp/473", "solution": "def tuple_intersection(list_of_tuples_1: list, list_of_tuples_2: list) -> set:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the intersection of two lists of tuples, ignoring element order.\n    Returns a set containing unique common tuples in canonical (sorted) form.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _normalize_tuple(t: tuple) -> tuple:\n        \"\"\"Sorts elements within a tuple to create a canonical representation.\"\"\"\n        return tuple(sorted(t))\n\n    canonical_set_1 = {_normalize_tuple(tup) for tup in list_of_tuples_1}\n    canonical_set_2 = {_normalize_tuple(tup) for tup in list_of_tuples_2}\n\n    return canonical_set_1.intersection(canonical_set_2)"}
