{"task_id": "Mbpp/559", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum(numbers: list[int], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the sum of the largest contiguous sublist using Kadane's algorithm.\n    The parameter 'n' indicates the length of the input 'numbers' list.\n    \"\"\"\n    global_max_sum = float('-inf') # Stores the maximum sum found across all sublists.\n    current_max_sum = 0            # Tracks the maximum sum of the sublist ending at the current position.\n\n    for num in numbers:\n        current_max_sum = max(num, current_max_sum + num)\n        global_max_sum = max(global_max_sum, current_max_sum)\n\n    return global_max_sum"}
