{"task_id": "Mbpp/564", "solution": "def count_Pairs(input_list: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of possible unordered pairs where both elements are unequal.\n    Generates all unique unordered pairs and filters those with unequal elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n    if n < 2:\n        return 0\n\n    unique_pairs = set()\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            element1 = input_list[i]\n            element2 = input_list[j]\n            if element1 != element2:\n                # Use frozenset to represent an unordered pair uniquely\n                unique_pairs.add(frozenset({element1, element2}))\n\n    return len(unique_pairs)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/562", "solution": "def Find_Max_Length(input_list_of_lists: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the length of the longest sublist within a list of lists.\n    Returns 0 if the input list is empty or contains only empty sublists.\"\"\"\n    max_length = 0\n    for sublist in input_list_of_lists:\n        current_length = len(sublist)\n        if current_length > max_length:\n            max_length = current_length\n    return max_length"}
