{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "def heap_sort(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of comparable items in ascending order using the heap sort algorithm.\n    It returns a new list containing the sorted items.\n    \"\"\"\n    arr = list(input_list) # Create a copy to avoid modifying the original list\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    # Helper function to maintain the max-heap property\n    def _heapify(arr: list, n: int, i: int):\n        largest = i\n        left = 2 * i + 1\n        right = 2 * i + 2\n\n        if left < n and arr[left] > arr[largest]:\n            largest = left\n\n        if right < n and arr[right] > arr[largest]:\n            largest = right\n\n        if largest != i:\n            arr[i], arr[largest] = arr[largest], arr[i]\n            _heapify(arr, n, largest)\n\n    # Build a max-heap (rearrange array)\n    for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n        _heapify(arr, n, i)\n\n    # One by one extract elements from heap\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        # Move current root to end\n        arr[i], arr[0] = arr[0], arr[i]\n        # Call _heapify on the reduced heap\n        _heapify(arr, i, 0)\n\n    return arr"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/638", "solution": "import math\ndef wind_chill(velocity, temperature):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the wind chill index given wind velocity in km/h and temperature in Celsius.\n    The result is rounded down to the nearest integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    v_power_0_16 = math.pow(velocity, 0.16)\n\n    wci_raw = (\n        13.12\n        + (0.6215 * temperature)\n        - (11.37 * v_power_0_16)\n        + (0.3965 * temperature * v_power_0_16)\n    )\n\n    return math.floor(wci_raw)"}
