{"task_id": "Mbpp/644", "solution": "def reverse_Array_Upto_K(arr: list, k: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Reverses an array up to a given 1-based position K, returning a new list.\"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input array must not be null or empty.\")\n    if not isinstance(k, int) or k <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Position K must be a positive integer.\")\n    if k > len(arr):\n        raise ValueError(\"Position K must not exceed the total number of elements in the array.\")\n\n    # Create a shallow copy to avoid modifying the original list\n    modified_arr = list(arr)\n\n    # Slice the part to be reversed (from index 0 up to k-1)\n    segment_to_reverse = modified_arr[:k]\n\n    # Reverse the segment\n    segment_to_reverse.reverse()\n\n    # Combine the reversed segment with the rest of the array\n    return segment_to_reverse + modified_arr[k:]"}
